      {
        "id": "p19-q1-j",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "j",
        "prompt": "$y=(x-3)(x-2)$ and $3x+2y=6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(\\tfrac32,\\tfrac34)$ and $(2,0)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x-3)(x-2)&=3-\\frac32x\\\\2x^2-10x+12&=6-3x\\\\2x^2-7x+6&=0\\\\(2x-3)(x-2)&=0\\\\x&=\\frac32,2\\end{align*}$$\nSubstituting into $y=3-\\tfrac32x$ gives $(\\tfrac32,\\tfrac34)$ and $(2,0)$. The parabola has intercepts $(2,0)$, $(3,0)$ and $(0,6)$ and vertex $(\\tfrac52,-\\tfrac14)$; the line has $y$-intercept $(0,3)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p19-q1-j-solution-graph",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"curveBlue\",\"hex\":\"268CFF\",\"reason\":\"parabola\"},{\"name\":\"lineRed\",\"hex\":\"EF6068\",\"reason\":\"line\"}],\"reference\":\"p19 1(j)\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=0.65cm]\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}\\definecolor{lineRed}{HTML}{EF6068}\\draw[->,line width=0.5pt](-0.7,0)--(4.5,0)node[fill=white,inner sep=1pt,right]{$x$};\\draw[->,line width=0.5pt](0,-2.8)--(0,7)node[fill=white,inner sep=1pt,above]{$y$};\\draw[curveBlue,line width=0.8pt,domain=-0.1:4.1,samples=100]plot(\\x,{(\\x-3)*(\\x-2)});\\draw[lineRed,line width=0.8pt](-0.5,3.75)--(3.7,-2.55);\\fill(1.5,0.75)circle(1.4pt)node[fill=white,inner sep=1pt,above right]{$(\\frac32,\\frac34)$};\\fill(2,0)circle(1.4pt)node[fill=white,inner sep=1pt,below left]{$(2,0)$};\\fill(3,0)circle(1.2pt)node[fill=white,inner sep=1pt,below right]{$(3,0)$};\\fill(0,3)circle(1.2pt)node[fill=white,inner sep=1pt,left]{$(0,3)$};\\fill(0,6)circle(1.2pt)node[fill=white,inner sep=1pt,right]{$(0,6)$};\\end{tikzpicture}",
